WEBVTT

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:04.300
Tenacious Bunch

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.240
That's..

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:32.430
Hey!

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:33.590
Are you okay?

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.580
Snap out of it.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:37.110
Snap out of it!

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.330
There's no mistaking that it's from our galaxy.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:49.190
The we can go home!

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:50.200
Yes.

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:52.900
Really? We can finally go home!

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:58.450
But why did only this person escape?

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.200
Looks like he's comin' to.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:08.350
Where is this?

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:12.810
You were washed up on the rocks. Kaoru found you.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:13.600
Kaoru?

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.230
What are you doing?

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:25.340
They...

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.100
They?

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:27.890
Yeah!

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:37.900
Did they make it?

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.340
That tenacious bunch...

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:51.030
If they find you, you'll all be killed!

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:58.450
What do you mean by killed?

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.980
Aren't there any adults?

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.640
There sure are! There's an adult right here!

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:07.830
What's wrong with this brat?

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:09.360
Brat?

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.160
There's nobody here but us.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:18.210
We were swallowed up by a gravity storm during our school trip.

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:20.610
Don't tell me you're them.

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:23.650
Do you know about us?

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:25.230
Of course.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:28.860
The disappearance of students from Soria Academy...

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.190
...was big news across the galaxy.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.140
There's nobody who didn't know.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:40.680
The president of the Howard group put up prize money for whoever found and returned them.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:42.330
Papa did!

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:46.080
I see. Everyone's been worried.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:48.080
Dad... Mom...

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:50.500
More importantly, what were you saying?

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:59.280
If they're still alive, I'd better tell you about them.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:04.940
I'm Polt, the mechanic for the interstellar transport ship Orion.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:13.980
This was right after Orion reached colony B-3.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:18.210
Old Man Porte, we have permission to go ashore.

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:22.230
Go on ahead. I'm going to check things out here.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:26.240
What? It's started up again?

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:29.010
This is the engine room. What's going on?

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.050
Captain, we're not supposed to leave until tomorrow.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:34.750
This ship is departing immediately.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:50.840
Captain!

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:02.540
They were escaped prisoners from an interim prison.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:09.180
What happened after that?

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:17.800
Somehow the Orion left Colony B-3, but the police were hot on our tail.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:19.530
And then...

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:28.790
What's wrong?

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:31.450
The Gyrostabilizer's been taken out!

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:32.540
You, fix it.

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:35.050
I won't know if I can 'till I look.

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:36.250
What?

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:39.140
If you can't fix it, you're finished.

00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:42.210
What is it this time?

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:44.090
This is...

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:47.160
...a gravity storm!

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:49.040
A gravity storm?

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:49.940
Yes...

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:54.030
It was the first time I'd seen such a large gravity storm.

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:57.660
Naturally I was expecting the worst.

00:08:04.490 --> 00:08:08.460
But somehow the Orion made it through the gravity storm safely.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:16.450
Damn it!

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:19.110
That was when it happened.

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:25.560
The distress signal I sent.

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:28.040
So that explains it.

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:30.290
But they took advantage of that.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:31.940
What do we do, Brindo?

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:32.910
Leave it to me.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:36.510
This is the Orion. We received your distress signal.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:41.950
--Hello? Hello?
--And they found out that you have a Gyrostabilizer...

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:44.310
Hey, Gramps.

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:48.060
Take care of the ship until we get to where they are.

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:53.280
They were after our Gyrostabilizer.

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:55.040
Yes.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:58.560
But I wouldn't give up hope.

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.580
If I fixed the ship, they'd just kill me anyway.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:04.580
So there was only one thing to do.

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:10.860
I broke all the other pods, leaving only my own.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:25.860
Now!

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:29.240
You know the rest.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.460
That was your escape pod then, Porte.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:33.400
Oh yeah...

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:35.280
I'd forgotten, but...

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:36.700
Here.

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:39.210
A gravity control unit!

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:44.200
You said you didn't have one, so I swiped the transport ship's spare.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:46.600
So, where's your ship?

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:50.540
Our shuttle's long since broken.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:53.650
It won't function as a ship anymore.

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:55.040
But...

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:58.790
...we have Adam's spaceship.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:00.140
Adam?

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:00.960
Yes.

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:04.940
Adam is of another species.

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.830
Another species?

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:13.080
Nice to meet you, kid.

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:16.900
Well, should we get going?

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:20.840
When the storm clears, they'll come ashore.

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:24.850
Let's fix the ship and get off this planet before that happens.

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:26.500
Let's hurry.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.730
If we leave now, the rain will wash away our footprints.

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.840
We won't have to worry about them catching up with us.

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.080
Thanks.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:36.080
I'll stay behind and keep an eye on them.

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:38.950
Be careful.

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:40.040
Yeah.

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:03.510
These are pretty impressive trees.

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:08.310
It was caused by the gravity unit on Adam's ship failing.

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.110
It's not just the vegetation.

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:13.340
The insects and animals are stupidly big.

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:14.840
Animals too?

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:18.060
Don't worry about it! I'm here, after all.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:20.800
Hey, say something!

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:37.530
You mean this is a space ship?

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:38.540
Yes.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:41.010
This is...

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:56.950
Hey, Gramps!

00:11:58.040 --> 00:11:59.240
This way.

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:08.880
This is the cockpit?

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:14.240
Huh? What's wrong, Gramps?

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:19.940
My mechanic skills are of use!

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:25.230
Is this geezer okay?

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:35.610
The basic systems seem just like mine.

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:36.360
Don't they?

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:39.250
But it's well done.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:42.890
Stop just admiring it and hurry up and fix it!

00:12:42.890 --> 00:12:44.200
Novice ??

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:46.710
The first thing is to inspect everything.

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:49.110
Everything starts from there.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.110
Outsiders, shut up!

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:52.080
Outsiders?

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:58.680
I see. This is the Gyrostabilizer, right?

00:12:58.830 --> 00:13:00.100
In that case...

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:07.040
Take this...

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:08.840
Yes, yes...

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:12.890
This is fine.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:20.090
Okay, I've pretty much figured it out.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:22.090
Well, let's get started.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:32.760
My toolkit.

00:13:32.990 --> 00:13:35.350
That's amazing, Porte!

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:36.850
What is?

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:40.790
Well, first we should take out the gravity control unit.

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:42.060
Okay!

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:45.510
I hope this going well.

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:05.310
Put this there.

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:05.950
Okay.

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:08.010
Right. And next is... here.

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:08.610
Here?

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:10.040
Yes. Take that.

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:11.950
Good work, kid.

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:13.490
I'm not a kid.

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:15.810
How about this?

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:20.990
Is it okay?

00:14:20.990 --> 00:14:21.740
Yep.

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:29.760
Great, now it should be okay.

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:31.300
Is it fixed?

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:32.990
Don't be impatient.

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:35.310
Well, here we go.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:42.480
Polt...

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:46.380
Won't it move even a little?

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:50.280
It's strange... that should have worked fine.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:52.790
How about now?

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:54.850
One more time!

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:55.900
Okay!

00:15:01.340 --> 00:15:03.550
It won't be so easy after all, I suppose.

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:05.840
Getting our hopes up...

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:11.460
Where's the problem?

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.800
It's mostly settled down.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.540
They may start to move.

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:32.500
Isn't it done yet?

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:35.880
If you're just gonna complain, go outside 'till you calm down!

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:51.930
Okay, give it a try.

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:53.010
Right.

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:54.890
Okay, here we go.

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:05.240
You're just going to fail again anyways.

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:06.180
Howard!

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:26.540
Is it working?

00:16:30.140 --> 00:16:32.460
Keep going... keep going...

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:34.900
Just like that!

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:41.650
Like I said, they failed.

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:44.130
It's impossible to fix after all.

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:46.710
Howard!

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:49.230
More importantly, I had a good idea.

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:50.280
Good idea?

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:52.110
Yeah.

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.940
We give this Gyrostabilizer back to them.

00:16:55.940 --> 00:16:56.730
What did you say?

00:16:56.840 --> 00:16:59.580
If we do that, <i>we</i> won't be able to fly!

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:03.360
Why not? It can't fly anyways.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:09.630
We give them the Gyrostabilizer and catch a lift with them.

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:13.260
That's the only way to escape from this planet!

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:14.650
That's naive.

00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:15.440
What?

00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:18.060
They only take what they want.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:20.910
They're not the kind of guys who'd let us hitch a lift.

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:23.460
That's where negotiation comes in.

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:24.930
Negotiation?

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:27.440
Didn't this geezer say?

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:30.930
We're famous around the galaxy.

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:33.250
They must know too.

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:37.600
If they take me home, they'll get the reward money from Papa.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:41.130
If they have a reason to save us, there's no way they'd kill us!

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:43.450
But they're escaped prisoners.

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:45.290
It's too dangerous.

00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:46.900
I'm opposed.

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:50.950
I think we should let Porte try a little longer.

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:54.250
Even if they've come ashore...

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:56.540
...they won't get here right away.

00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:58.540
We still have time.

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:00.250
Then I guess it's decided.

00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:02.010
Leave it to me!

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:04.000
This time we'll get it working!

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:05.950
Do what you want.

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:09.330
Luna!

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:10.600
What's wrong?

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:12.890
The storm... the storm cleared!

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:14.540
What'd you say?

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:23.350
Bell...

00:18:54.740 --> 00:18:56.540
It seems to have calmed down.

00:18:56.950 --> 00:19:02.050
Then shall we go take their Gyrostabilizer?

00:19:05.010 --> 00:19:06.510
We're ready to go.

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:08.840
Let's go!

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:17.840
Here they come.

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:22.230
Damn that geezer.

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:24.510
When we find him he's in for a world of hurt.

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:21.360
A laser gun?

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:27.360
What was that?

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:29.580
This is an interesting planet.

00:20:35.090 --> 00:20:36.290
He's laughing it up!

00:20:57.930 --> 00:20:59.460
Looks like the old man was with them.

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:03.030
It's great to be free again.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:04.150
Anything there?

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:06.780
Looks like there used to be.

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:09.480
They even took the cloth off the seats.

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:14.390
Which means they have another ship where their Gyrostabilizer is.

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:15.290
Yeah.

00:21:16.490 --> 00:21:17.430
Probably.

00:21:20.730 --> 00:21:21.660
Let's go!

00:21:30.360 --> 00:21:32.760
A laser gun and an electric whip.

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:35.990
And the big one is a cyborg.

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:52.000
How is it?

00:21:52.150 --> 00:21:54.250
Looks like it'll still take a little while.

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:55.680
Really...

00:21:56.840 --> 00:21:58.490
I wonder if Kaoru's okay.

00:22:05.350 --> 00:22:06.480
Kaoru!

00:22:11.880 --> 00:22:13.940
They're at Everyone's House?

00:22:14.050 --> 00:22:14.580
Yeah.

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:19.230
But I can't believe they took out that sea snake in one shot.

00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:22.040
It seems wise to stay away from them.

00:22:26.200 --> 00:22:26.990
Where's Howard?

00:22:27.480 --> 00:22:30.030
Come to think of it, he's been gone a while.

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:33.030
He's just gone back there to goof off.

00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:34.680
I hope so, but...

00:22:40.860 --> 00:22:43.750
Like I'd leave it to them any longer!

00:23:03.630 --> 00:23:08.840
Oh no! Howard's gone to negotiate with the escaped prisoners in secret!

00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:12.400
He took an important part with him!

00:23:12.480 --> 00:23:15.700
If the space ship can't fly, what'll we do?

00:23:16.300 --> 00:23:17.800
I'm worried about Howard.

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:19.230
We have to do something!

00:23:20.130 --> 00:23:22.490
Even if he's that kind of guy, he's our friend.

00:23:22.640 --> 00:23:24.550
He's a real troublesome guy!

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:28.560
Next time: This is for everyone's sake too.
